{
 "title": "This desert was a sea",
 "narration": "This desert was a sea. And the ships are still here. In nineteen sixty, the Aral Sea was the fourth largest lake on Earth, almost the size of Ireland. Two rivers kept it alive. Then Soviet planners wanted cotton. They turned both rivers into the desert, and the sea began to starve. The port of Moynaq watched the water walk away, year after year, until its fishing boats sat rusting in the sand. By two thousand seven, nine tenths of the sea was gone. But in the north, Kazakhstan built one dam, and the water came back. So the sea did not die. We turned it off.",
